# Pin this repo to the public npm registry.
#
# Without this, installing from inside the corporate network writes
# `resolved` URLs pointing at the internal Nexus mirror
# (http://nexus3.weg.net/repository/npm-group) into package-lock.json. 261 of
# them had already accumulated there. Those URLs are unreachable from a GitHub
# Actions runner and unauthenticated inside the Docker build, so `npm ci` fails
# with E401 in both — while `npm install` on a developer laptop keeps working,
# which is what let it go unnoticed.
#
# Package `integrity` hashes are registry-independent, so a lockfile normalised
# to this registry still verifies byte-for-byte.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
